# Claude Code session material: maintainer notes and scratch, kept per working tree and
# never published. Unanchored, so a CLAUDE.md in any subfolder is covered too.
TODO.md
CLAUDE.md
CLAUDE.local.md

# Per-machine settings. The .example files are tracked; the real ones are not.
etc/amphora.local
# The pre-Amphora name. amphoractl refuses to run while it exists, but a stale copy
# still holds phone numbers and addresses and must never be committed.
etc/hermes.local
etc/mounts
etc/feeds.csv
# The list's tab-separated predecessor. A stale copy still names one machine's sources.
etc/feeds.tsv
# The temporary copy `amphoractl signal groups` writes beside amphora.local; it holds
# everything that file does.
etc/amphora.local.tmp.*

# Written by `up` at the runtime folder's root, which is the checkout when
# AMPHORA_RUNTIME_DIR is unset. It names this checkout's path on this machine.
.amphora-stack

# Secrets live in podman's secret store, never here — this is belt and braces.
.env
.env.*
*.key
*.pem
auth.json

# Agent workspace: one sub-folder per project, each typically its own repo.
projects/

# The agent's own skills: personal to one deployment, and written by the agent.
/skills/

# Hermes state lives in podman volumes, but guard against a stray bind mount.
.hermes/
data/
logs/
tmp/

# Volume snapshots from `amphoractl backup`.
#
# DO NOT REMOVE. A snapshot is a byte-for-byte copy of /opt/data: every session, memory,
# skill and kanban card the agent holds, including anything it was ever told in
# confidence. Committing one cannot be undone by deleting it later — the objects stay in
# history and in every clone. `amphoractl backup` also writes backups/.gitignore as a
# second line of defence, and `amphoractl doctor` fails if this entry stops working.
backups/

# Files the agent sent over Signal or email, from /mounts/outbox. Whatever it was asked
# to send.
outbox/

# Superseded agent output, copied out of projects/ before a rerun overwrites it. Same
# class as projects/ — agent-generated content, not stack material — and it can carry
# whatever the agent was researching, so it is not tracked here.
archive/

# Session handovers. Each names real addresses, domains and numbers for one machine, and
# each says in its own header that it stays out of git — this is what makes that true.
HANDOVER-*.md

# Scratch output from Claude Code sessions; not stack material.
Claude outputs/
.claude/

# Python bytecode, from running the sweep in tools/.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Editor state: per-person, and it can record local paths.
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
